      "raw": "No - each hit is a separate instance of damage, even if it&#39;s in the same power (eg Fanatic&#39;s Exorcism or Jim&#39;s Compounded Bow). As such, if someone&#39;s damage is boosted, the boost applies to both plinks of damage. The only time this wouldn&#39;t be the case is if a certain damage [i]type[/i] is boosted and the attack consists of both that type and another - say there was something boosting all infernal damage (there isn&#39;t, but just as an example) and Jim fired his Bow - the first hit is projectile so wouldn&#39;t get a boost. But then the second hit can be any type he likes, so he decides to make it infernal, so it gets the +1 and becomes two points of damage.\n",
