    {
      "id": 108468,
      "name": "JimB",
      "username": "JimB",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jimb/{size}/2093_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-07-05T14:45:52.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So here’s a related question: Expatriette’s Shock Rounds in conjunction with a Submachine Gun.  The text reads, “When that card’s power is used to damage a target, Expatriette deals each non-hero target 1 lightning damage.”  Until last night, I’d taken that to mean that the extra damage occurs per power use; so essentially, this combo does 1+1 damage to every non-hero on the board.  Last night, though, I realized I could, with a clean conscience, take it to key off instances of damage, so that every time a target is damaged, every valid target takes 1 lightning damage and the total damage is something more like [1 + number of non-hero targets, assuming they all have enough HP for the experience] to each valid target.</p>\n<p>So which is it, a flat 1 to everyone, or a scaling number of +1s?</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:38:57.835Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 10673,
      "topic_slug": "doubled-damage-modifiers",
      "display_username": "JimB",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
