      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "So here's a related question: Expatriette's Shock Rounds in conjunction with a Submachine Gun.  The text reads, \"When that card's power is used to damage a target, Expatriette deals each non-hero target 1 lightning damage.\"  Until last night, I'd taken that to mean that the extra damage occurs per power use; so essentially, this combo does 1+1 damage to every non-hero on the board.  Last night, though, I realized I could, with a clean conscience, take it to key off instances of damage, so that every time a target is damaged, every valid target takes 1 lightning damage and the total damage is something more like [1 + number of non-hero targets, assuming they all have enough HP for the experience] to each valid target.\r\n\r\nSo which is it, a flat 1 to everyone, or a scaling number of +1s?",
      "actions_summary": [
